  "notes": [
    "Regular -AR verb — follows standard -AR endings with no exceptions",
    "Past participle: *limado* (regular)",
    "Means \"to file\" (nails, metal) or \"to smooth/polish\" — *limarse las uñas* (to file one's nails, with reflexive *limarse*), *limar el metal* (to file down the metal)",
    "Also used figuratively to mean \"to smooth over\" (differences, conflicts): *limar las asperezas* (to smooth things over, to iron out differences)",
    "Related: *lima* (file, the tool — also \"lime,\" the fruit, a different word with the same spelling), *limadura* (filings)"
  ],
